{"date":"2026-11-15","caps":[[0.05,"Arnie Jordan here, coming to you from row three at Jordan Arena, with the Rinkside Report."],[5.14,"And this week, for the first time ever, you can see me! That's right, the Rinkside Report is on camera."],[10.95,"The camera is my nephew's iPad, propped up on my coffee cup and held there with a roll of hockey tape."],[16.71,"It took him forty minutes to find me the record button. So wave. Two of you, maybe three. Hi."],[22.6,"Sunday, November fifteenth."],[24.15,"Last week my nephew said we try crayons, so I came with the notebook and the big box. Sixty-four colours!"],[30.01,"Thirty-seven goals. You'd think that's plenty. You would be wrong."],[34.34,"The early game, the J.E. Culp Habs against the Timbit Senators."],[37.83,"Dixon opened it, Williams tied it, and Tuby put the Habs back up."],[41.44,"Then, with two seconds left in the first, Greg Penney scored all by himself. Two seconds."],[46.35,"That's not a goal, that's a doorbell ditch."],[49.39,"Then the Habs hit the buffet. KP, thirty-six seconds into the second. Holt got one back. Cooke. Deakin."],[55.06,"Then Greg Penney, Tuby and Dixon, three goals in three minutes, and Chinner made it nine to three."],[60.46,"By then I'd used red, blue, white, a second red, and Burnt Sienna. I don't know what Burnt Sienna is."],[66.02,"Buynink came out of the Senators net for Shannon halfway through, and the Habs said welcome, here's six more."],[72.67,"In the third, Williams and Simon Murphy made it nine to six. Then Hunt, and Ort. Eleven to six, final."],[78.29,"Tuby had five points."],[79.49,"And Ort scored, set one up, and took three for roughing at the exact same second Schmidt took three for slashing."],[85.71,"Those two weren't battling, they were synchronizing watches."],[89.68,"Game two, The Keg Canucks against Dawson's Oilers. Adam Short and Beckett put the Canucks up two nothing."],[95.57,"Then the second period became the McPherson Show. McPherson from Mansion."],[99.68,"McPherson again, tie game, and on that same second both teams changed goalies."],[104.71,"Snihur went off for tripping, and the Canucks scored anyway. Koke, short-handed, from Pundy and Goodie."],[110.26,"McPherson got it back on the power play, three all. Then the Oilers got caught with too many men."],[115.5,"NoPants hopped over the boards, Wall never came off, and HoundDog got to sit three minutes for the both of them."],[121.53,"NoPants, Wall, it's a line change, not a carpool."],[124.2,"Colin Murphy scored right after it ran out, from Adam Short and Wes Short."],[128.2,"The Short to Short connection now comes with a Murphy extension."],[132.32,"McPherson tied it four all in the third. Four goals, every Oiler goal, and Mansion helped on all four."],[137.82,"That's not a line, that's a two-man band. Then New Guy scored, and a minute later New Guy scored again."],[143.36,"Six to four Canucks, and that's the Canucks' first win of the season! Somebody frame the score sheet."],[148.8,"McPherson, four goals and a loss. That's catching four fish and the boat sinks."],[153.06,"And Dawson gave up four in front of a team named after him. Nobody respects the landlord."],[158.47,"The late game, the ColdBreak Leafs against the RegattaSport Nordiques. Pierce scored twenty-seven seconds in."],[164.29,"Brophy went off for hooking, and Lawrence scored short-handed anyway. Two short-handed goals in one night."],[169.94,"I don't own a crayon for that. Then Pierce got the power-play goal, from Steele. Two to one Leafs."],[175.8,"In the second, Collini went off for slashing, and the Nordiques made it count."],[180.26,"Rob DeBolster scored while he sat, and thirty-five seconds later Dykstra, three to two Nordiques."],[185.78,"Collini, one slash, two goals against. Bad exchange rate."],[189.05,"Mallet came out for Rosie, JMAC came out for Trigg, and Pulo made it four to two with fifty-eight seconds left in the period."],[196.81,"Langlois scored early in the third. Larry Penney got one back."],[200.14,"Then Moorzey scored from Regular and Lawrence, and on that same second, Brophy went off for roughing."],[205.52,"Brophy, up by three and you still needed a sit-down. Six minutes, most of anybody all night."],[210.44,"Horton got one more for the Leafs, and that was it. Six to four Nordiques."],[215.02,"Somewhere in there, a clearing attempt went so high it rang off the clock."],[218.82,"I didn't catch who shot it, and I'm not asking."],[221.9,"Now, a look at the big board, seven games in."],[224.58,"The scoring race: McPherson leads with nineteen points, and right behind him, KP, Pierce and Moorzey are all tied at eighteen."],[231.97,"Three fellas at eighteen. That's not a race, that's a traffic jam."],[235.87,"In net, by goals against average, JMAC is on top at three twenty-five, Trigg is right behind him at three thirty-one, and Dawson is third at three forty-two."],[245.06,"The Nordiques' top two goalies share one crease. Cozy."],[248.88,"And the standings."],[249.9,"The Nordiques are seven and oh, fourteen points, perfect, and I'm running out of nice things to say."],[255.36,"The Oilers are second with nine."],[257.14,"The Habs and Leafs are tied with seven, the Senators have six, and the Canucks have two, both from last night."],[263.14,"You've got to start somewhere, boys."],[265.77,"So that's your week."],[266.93,"Eleven for the Habs, four for McPherson in a loss, and a New Guy who scored two and is still the New Guy."],[272.78,"By the late game I was writing Nordiques goals in Mauve. My nephew says next week, a whiteboard."],[278.14,"If I got your name wrong, or gave your goal to the fella beside you, take it up with the refs, the timekeeper, and how fast you guys skate out there."],[286.42,"Tape your sticks. This has been Arnie Jordan with the Rinkside Report."]],"pages":[["ROW 3 - 11/15","ON CAMERA!!","iPad + hockey tape","coffee = tripod"],["64 crayons","nephew: trust me","37 goals??"],["G1: Habs @ Sens","Habs 3 - Sens 1","Culp: 2 assists","D